hadiths[166]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2133","Asim bin 'Ubaidullah said:' I heard Salim bin 'Abdullah narrating a Hadith from his father who said: \'Umar said : \""O Messenger of Allah! Do you see that what we do is a new matter- or a matter initiated – or it is a matter already concluded?” He (s.a.w) said: “ O Ibn Al-Khattab! It is a matter already concluded. For everyone is suited (for that for which he is created). As for one who is among the people of happiness"""
"2134","Ali narrated:\We were with the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) and he was scraping the ground"""
"2135","Abdullah bin Mas'ud said:The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) narrated to us - and he is the truthful and entrusted one: 'Indeed the creation of one of you is gathered inside his mother in forty days. Then"
"2136","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Every child is born upon the Millah"""
"2137","Salman narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Nothing turns back the Decree except supplication"""
"2138","Anas narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) would often say: Ya Muqallibal-qulub"""
"2139","Abdullah bin 'Amr narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) came out to us with two books in hand. And he said: 'Do you know what these two books are?' We said: 'No"""
"2140","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\When Allah wants good for a slave"""
"2141","Ibn Mas'ud narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) stood among us and said: 'One thing does not infect another.' So a Bedouin said: 'O Messenger of Allah! If a camel gets mangy glands and we leave it at the resting place of camels"""
"2142","Jabir bin 'Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:'A slave (of Allah) shall not believe until he believes in Al-Qadar"
"2143","Ali narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:'A slave (of Allah) shall not believe until he believes in four: The testimony of La Ilaha Illallah"
"2144","Matar bin 'Ukamis narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\When Allah decrees that a slave (of His) is to die in a land"""
"2145","Abu 'Azzah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\When Allah decrees that a slave (of His) is to die in a land"""
"2146","**Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us, Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatādah, from Abū ʿAbdullāh, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allāh be pleased with him), that the Prophet ﷺ used to prescribe olive oil and wars¹ for the treatment of *dhāt al-janb* (pleurisy).\n\n**Qatādah said:** \And he would apply it to the side from which the patient was suffering.\""\n\n**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** \""This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* hadith. And Abū ʿAbdullāh's name is Maymūn; he is a Basran shaykh.\""\n

\n1. **Wars** (الورس): A plant known as *Memecylon tinctorium* or a type of safflower-like dye plant"
"2147","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\There are two groups in my Ummah for whom there is no share in Islam: The Murji'ah and the Qadariyyah.\"" Another chain reports a similar narration"""
"2148","Ibn Abi Khizamah narrated from his father,that a man came to the Prophet(s.a.w) and said:""O Messenger of Allah! Do you think that the Ruqyah we use, the treatments we use, and what we seek to protect ourselves with prevent anything from Allah's Decree?' He said: 'They are from Allah's Decree"
"2149","Sa'd narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:'From (the signs of) the son of Adam's prosperity"
"2150","Nafi' narrated that a man came to Ibn 'Umar and said:\So-and-so conveys his Salam to you.\"" So he said: \""It has been conveyed to me that he has innovated"""
"2151","Ibn 'Umar narrated from the Prophet (s.a.w):\There will be a collapse of the earth and transformation in my Ummah"""
"2152","Nafi' narrated that a man came to Ibn 'Umar and said:""So-and-so conveys his Salam to you."" So he said: ""It has been conveyed to me that he has innovated, so if he has indeed innovated, then do not convey my Salam to him, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) saying: 'In this Ummah' or: 'In my Ummah'"" - the doubt was his - ""a collapse of the earth, or a transformation, or stones shall rain upon the people of Al-Qadr"
"2153","Abdul-Wahid bin Sulaim narrated:\I arrived in Makkah and met 'Ata bin Abi Rabah. I said to him: 'O Abu Muhammad! The people of Al-Basrah speak about Al-Qadar.' He said: 'O my son! Do you recite the Quran?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then recite Az-Zukhruf to me.'\"" He said: 'So I recited: Ha Mim. By the manifest Book. Verily"""
"2154","Abdullah bin 'Amr narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Allah decreed the measures fifty-thousand years before He created the Heavens and the earth"""
"2155","'Abd Allah ibn Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, saying: 'Uqbah ibn Khalid al-Sakuni narrated to us, from Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When you visit a sick person"
"2156","Hannad and Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Isma'il ibn 'Ubayd Allah, from Abu Salih al-Ash'ari, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) visited a man suffering from a fever and said: \Good news! For Allah says: 'It is My fire"
"2157","Abu Hurairah said:\Idolaters from the Quraish came to the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) quarreling about Al-Qadar. So this Ayah was revealed: \""The day they will be dragged on their faces into the Fire (it will be said to them): \""Taste you the touch of Hell.\"" Verily we have created all things with Qadar"""
"2158","Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif narrated that on the day of siege, 'Uthman bin 'Affan stood overlooking the people, and he said:""I swear to you by Allah! You know that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said: 'The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful, except for one of three (cases):Illegitimate sexual relations after Ihsan (having been married), or apostasy after Islam, or taking a life without right, for which he is killed.'	By Allah! I have never committed illegitimate sexual relations, not during Jahiliyyah nor during Islam, and I have not committed apostasy since I gave my pledge to the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w), and I have not taken a life that Allah had made unlawful. So for what do you fight me?"
"2159","Sulaiman bin 'Amr bin Al-Ahwas narrated from his father who said:\During the Farewell Pilgrimage"""
"2160","**Narrated by al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah, who said:** Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu Qays al-Awdi, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, who said:\n\nA man came to Abu Musa and Salman ibn Rabi'ah and asked them about the share of the daughter, the daughter of the son, and the full sister. They said: \The daughter receives one-half"
"2161","Muhammad bin Yusuf narrated that As-Sa'ib bin Yazid said:\Yazid performed Hajj in the Farewell Pilgrimage with the Prophet (s.a.w) when I was seven years old.\"" So 'Ali bin Al-Madini narrated from Yahya bin Sa'eed Al-Qattan: \""Muhammad bin Yusuf was a very reliable narrator of Hadith"""
"2162","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\Whoever points a piece of iron at his brother"""
"2163","Jabir narrated :\The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) prohibited passing an unsheathed sword"""
"2164","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:""Whoever prays Subh, then he is under the protection of Allah's covenant, so do not infringe at all upon Allah's covenant"
"2165","Ibn 'Umar narrated:\ 'Umar delivered a Khutbah to us at Al-Jabiyah. He said: 'O you people! Indeed I have stood among you as the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) stood among us"""
"2166","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Allah's Hand is with the Jama'ah"""
"2167","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:'Indeed Allah will not gather my Ummah \ - or he said: \""[Muhammad's]Ummah upon deviation"""
"2168","Abu Bakr As-Siddiq said:\O you people! You recite this Ayah: Take care of yourselves! If you follow the guidance no harm shall come to you. I indeed heard the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) saying: 'When the people see the wrongdoer and they do not take him by the hand"""
"2169","Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! Either you command good and forbid evil"""
"2170","Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! The Hour will not be established until you fight your A'immah"""
"2171","Umm Salamah narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) mentioned the army that the earth would swallow"
"2172","Tariq bin Shihab said:\The first to advance the Khutbah before the Salat was Marwan. A man stood to say to Marwan: 'You have contradicted the Sunnah.' So he said: 'O so-and-so! What was there it has been left.' So Abu Sa'eed said: 'As for this"""
"2173","An-Nu'man bin Bashir narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\The parable of the one who upholds Allah's laws and the one who breaches them"""
"2174","Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi and others narrated to us: They said: Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri... And Ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to us similarly. Abu 'Isa said: And in this chapter there are narrations from Jabir and 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr. And this is a hasan sahih hadith. Thus Ma'mar and others narrated from al-Zuhri similarly. And Malik narrated from al-Zuhri, from 'Ali ibn al-Husayn, from 'Umar ibn 'Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from the Prophet ﷺ similarly. And Malik's hadith is a mistake; Malik erred in it. And some narrated it from Malik saying: from 'Amr ibn 'Uthman. And most of Malik's companions said: from Malik, from 'Umar ibn 'Uthman. And 'Amr ibn 'Uthman ibn 'Affan is well-known among the descendants of 'Uthman, and 'Umar ibn 'Uthman is not known. And the practice is upon this hadith among the people of knowledge. And some people of knowledge differed concerning the inheritance of the apostate. Most of the people of knowledge from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and others made the wealth for his Muslim heirs. And some said: His Muslim heirs do not inherit him, and they argued with the hadith of the Prophet ﷺ: ""The Muslim does not inherit the disbeliever, nor does the disbeliever inherit the Muslim."" And it is the view of al-Shafi'i."
"2175","Abdullah bin Khabbab bin Al-Aratt narrated from his father:\The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) performed Salat"""
"2176","Thawban narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Indeed Allah gathered the earth for me so that I saw its east and its west. And surely my Ummah's authority shall reach over all that was shown to me of it. And I have been granted the two treasures; the red and the white. I asked my Lord that my Ummah is not to be destroyed by a universal drought"""
"2177","Umm Malik Al-Bahziyyah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) mentioned Fitnah"
"2178","Abdullah bin 'Amr narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\There shall be a Fitnah of extermination of the 'Arabs. Its fighters are in the Fire. During it"""
"2179","Hudhaifah [bin Al-Yaman] said:\The Messenger of Allah {s.a.w} narrated two narrations to us"""
"2180","Abu Waqid Al-Laithi narrated that when the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) went out to Hunain he passed a tree that the idolaters called Dhat Anwat upon which they hung their weapons. They(the Companions) said:\O Messenger of Allah! Make a Dhat Anwat for us as they have a Dhat Anwat.' The Prophet (s.a.w) said: \""Subhan Allah! This is like what Musa's people said: Make for us a god like their gods. By the One in Whose is my soul! You shall follow the way of those who were before you"""
"2181","Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! The Hour will not be established until predators speak to people and until the tip of a man's whip and the straps on his sandal speak to him"""
"2182","Ibn 'Umar said:\The moon split during the time of the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w)"""
"2183","Ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, who said: I fell ill during the Year of the Conquest with an illness that brought me to the brink of death. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit me. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth, and none inherits me except my daughter. Shall I bequeath all my wealth?"" He said: ""No."" I said: ""Then two-thirds of my wealth?"" He said: ""No."" I said: ""Then half?"" He said: ""No."" I said: ""Then a third?"" He said: ""A third, and a third is much. For if you leave your heirs rich, it is better than leaving them dependent, begging from people. And you will not spend any expenditure seeking Allah's Countenance thereby except you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you raise to your wife's mouth."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, shall I be left behind from my emigration (hijrah)?"" He said: ""You will not be left behind after me doing any deed seeking Allah's Face thereby except you will increase thereby in rank and degree. And perhaps you will be left behind so that some people may benefit by you and others be harmed by you. O Allah, cause my Companions' emigration to reach its goal and do not turn them back on their heels. But the wretched one is Sa'd ibn Khawlah,"" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pitied him because he died in Makkah. Abu 'Isa said: And in this chapter there is a narration from Ibn 'Abbas. And this is a hasan sahih hadith. And this hadith has been narrated from other chains from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas. And the practice is upon this among the people of knowledge: that it is not permissible for a man to bequeath more than a third. And some people of knowledge recommended reducing from the third because of the Prophet's ﷺ saying: ""And a third is much."""
"2184","Safiyyah narrated \The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:'The people will not finish attacking this House until it is attacked by an army which"""
"2185","Aishah narrated \The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:'In the end of this Ummah there will be a collapse"""
"2186","**Narrated by Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif:**\n\nHe said: \I asked Ibn Abī Awfā (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu)"
"2187","Zainab bint Jahsh said:\One day the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) awoke from sleep with a flushed red face"""
"2188","Abdullah [bin Mas'ud] narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\In the end of time there will come a people young in years"""
"2189","Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, narrated by Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from al-Harith, from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) decreed that the debt takes precedence over the bequest, whereas you recite the bequest before the debt. Abu 'Isa said: The practice according to the generality of the scholars is that the debt is given priority over the bequest."
"2190","**Narrated by Abu Habibah al-Ta'i:**\n\nMy brother bequeathed part of his estate to me. I met Abu al-Darda' and said, \My brother has bequeathed a portion of his wealth to me. Where do you advise me to distribute it—among the poor"
"2191","**Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah, that 'A'ishah رضي الله عنها informed him that Barirah came seeking the assistance of 'A'ishah رضي الله Regarding the payment of her manumission contract, and she had not yet paid anything of her contract. So 'A'ishah رضي الله عنها said to her: \Return to your family"
"2192","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\Give gifts"""
"2193","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W)said:\The parable of the one who gives a gift"""
"2194","Ibn 'Umar and Ibn 'Abbas narrated the Marfu Hadith:\It is not lawful for a man to give a gift and then take it back"""
"2195","Mu'awiyah bin Qurrah narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\When the inhabitants of Ash-Sham become corrupt"""
"2196","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\Do not revert to disbelief after me"""
"2197","Busr bin Sa'eed said:During the Fitnah(in the time) of 'Uthman bin 'Affan"
"2198","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\Rush to do good deeds. A Fitnah will occur that is like a portion of the dark night"""
"2199","Umm Salamah narrated:\One night the Prophet (ﷺ) awoke and said"""
"2200","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\Before the Hour there shall be Fitan like a portion of the dark night. Morning will come upon a man as a believer"""
"2201","Ma'qil bin Yasar narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:\Worship during Al-Harj is like Hijrah to me"""
"2202","Thawban narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\When the sword is imposed on my Ummah"""
"2203","Udaisah bint Uhban bin Safi Al-Ghifari said:\Ali bin Abi Talib came to my father to call him to go out(to fight) with him. My father said to him: 'Indeed my beloved"""
"2204","Narrated by al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥulwānī, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr and Wakīʿ narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, from ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:\n\n\While we were with the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him)"
"2205","Anas bin Malik said:\I shall narrate a Hadith to you that I heard from the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w)"""
"2206","Az-Zubair bin 'Adi said:\We entered upon Anas bin Malik. We complained to him about what we were experiencing from Al-Hajjaj. So he said: 'There will not be a year"""
"2207","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\The Hour will not be established until 'Allah"""
"2208","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\ The earth will throw out pieces of its liver(in sides): liver; gold and silver will come out like columns.\"" He said: \""A thief will come and say: 'For this my hands were amputated?' A murderer will come and say: 'For this I killed?' One who severed ties of kinship will come and say: 'For this I severed the ties of kinship?' Then they will leave it without taking anything from it"""
"2209","Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\The Hour will not be established until the happiest of people in the world is Luka' bin Luka"""
"2210","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\When my Ummah does fifteen things"""
"2211","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\When Al-Fai' is distributed(preferentially)"""
"2212","Imran bin Husain narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\In this Ummah there shall be collapsing of the earth"""
"2213","Al-Mustawrid bin Shaddad Al-Fihri reported that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\I was sent in advance of the Hour"""
"2214","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\The Hour and I were dispatched like these two\"" - and Abu Dawud(a narrator) indicated with his index and middle fingers- so"""
"2215","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:\The Hour shall not be established until you fight a people whose sandals are made out of hair"""
"2216","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\When Kisra is ruined"""
"2217","**Wāṣil ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā al-Kūfī narrated to us, saying:** Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us, from al-Qāsim ibn Ḥabīb and ʿAlī ibn Nizār, from Nizār, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said:\n\n**The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:**\n\n*\Two groups from my Ummah shall have no share in Islam: the Murji'ah and the Qadariyyah.\""*\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: **\""In this chapter"
"2218","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\The Hour shall not be established until nearly thirty imposters"""
"2219","Thawban narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\The Hour shall not be established until tribes of my Ummah unite with the idolaters"""
"2220","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\In Thaqif there will be a great liar and destroyer"""
"2221","Imran bin Husain narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\The best of people are my generation"""
"2222","Imran bin Husain narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\The best of my Ummah is the generation among whom I was sent"""
"2223","Simak bin Harb narrated from Jabir bin Samurah who said \ The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:'There will be twelve Amir after me.\""' He said: \""Then he said something that I did not understand. So I asked the one who was next to me"""
"2224","Ziyad bin Kusaib Al-'Adawi said:\I was with Abu Bakrah under the Minbar of Ibn 'Amir while he was giving a Khutbah wearing a fine garment. Abu Bilal said: 'Look at our Amir wearing clothes of wickedness!' So Abu Bakrah said: Be quiet! I heard the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) saying: \""Whoever insults Allah's Sultan on the earth"""
"2225","Salim bin 'Abdullah narrated from his father who said:\It was said to 'Umar bin Al-Khattab: 'Perhaps you should endorse your successor.' He said: 'If I appoint a successor"""
"2226","**Narration:**\n\nAḥmad ibn ʿAbdah al-Ḍabbī narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Abū Umāmah ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf, that **ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān** (رضي الله عنه), on the **Day of the House** (*Yawm al-Dār*), looked down over the wall and said:\n\n> \I adjure you by Allah — do you know that the **Messenger of Allah** (صلى الله عليه وسلم) said:\n>\n> *'The blood of a Muslim is not lawful except for one of three: adultery after marriage (*zinā baʿda iḥṣān*)"
"2227","Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hudhail said:\ There were some people from(the tribe of) Rabiah with 'Amr bin Al-'As"""
"2228","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\The night and the day shall not go away until a man called Jahjah among the Mawali reigns"""
"2229","Thawban narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\I only fear for my Ummah from the misguiding A'immah.\"" He said that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said: \""There will never cease to be a group from my Ummah manifest upon the truth"""
"2230","Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\The world shall not pass away until a man from the people of my family rules the Arabs whose name agrees with my name"""
"2231","**Narrated by 'Abdullāh ibn Mu'āwiyah al-Jumaḥī al-Baṣrī**, who narrated from **Ḥammād ibn Salamah**, from **Abū al-Zubayr**, from **Jābir** (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:\n\n> **The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that a sword be handed over while drawn (unsheathed).**\n\nAbū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: *\In this chapter (there is also a narration) from Abū Bakrah (may Allāh be pleased with him).\""*\n\nHe further said: *\""This is a **ḥasan gharīb** ḥadīth from the narration of Ḥammād ibn Salamah.\""*\n\nHe added: *\""Ibn Lahī'ah also narrated this ḥadīth from Abū al-Zubayr"
"2232","Zaid bin Al-'Ammi said:\I heard Abu As-Siddiq An-Naji narrate a Hadith from Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri who said: 'We feared events to occur after our Prophet"""
"2233","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:\By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! Ibn Mariam shall soon descend among you"""
"2234","Abu 'Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah said:\I heard the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w): 'There was never a Prophet after Nuh but that he warned his people about the Dajjal"""
"2235","Az-Zuhri narrated from Salim from Ibn 'Umar who said:\The Messengers of Allah(s.a.w)stood among the people"""
"2236","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\You shall fight the Jews. You will gain such control over them"""
"2237","Abu Bakr As-Siddiq said:\The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) narrated to us"""
"2238","Qutaybah narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr, from ʿAbd Allāh — who is Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Anṣārī al-Ashhalī — from Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān (may Allāh be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\By the One in Whose Hand is my soul"
"2239","Anas bin Malik said:\Constantinople will be conquered with the coming of the Hour"""
"2240","**Narrated by Bundār, who narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī, who narrated from Sufyān, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Ṭāriq ibn Shihāb, who said:**\n\n\The first person to deliver the sermon (*khutbah*) before the prayer was Marwān. A man stood up and said to Marwān"
"2241","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) was asked about the Dajjal, so he said:""Lo! Indeed your Lord is not blind in one eye, and indeed he is blind in one eye; his right eye is as if it is a floating grape"
"2242","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\The Dajjal will come to Al-Madinah to find the angels have surrounded it. Neither the plague nor the Dajjal will enter it"""
"2243","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""Faith is Yemeni, and disbelief is from the direction of the east. Tranquility is for the people of sheep, and wickedness and Riya is in those who boast among the people of horses and the people of camels. Al-Masih – that is Ad-Dajjal- will come, and when he reaches behind Uhud, the angels will turn his face to the direction of Ash-Sham, and is there that he will be destroyed.” (Sahih)"
"2244","Mujammi' bin Jariyah Al-Ansari said:\I heard the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) saying: 'Eisa bin Maryam will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd"""
"2245","It was narrated that Anas said:\The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said: 'There was no Prophet except that he warned his Ummah of the liar who is blind in one eye. Lo! He is blind in one eye"""
"2246","Abu Sa'eed said:\I was accompanied by Ibn Sa'eed- either performing Hajj or 'Umrah - the people departed"""
"2247","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed said:\The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) met Ibn Sa'eed on one of the streets of Al-Madinah"""
"2248","It was narrated from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Bakrah from his father who said:\The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said: 'The father of the Dajjal and hid mother"""
"2249","Narrated Sufyān ibn Wakīʿ, who narrated from his father, from al-Qāsim ibn al-Faḍl, from Abū Naḍrah al-ʿAbdī, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n\By the One in Whose Hand is my soul"
"2250","Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, from Shuʿbah, from al-Aʿmash, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said:\n\n\The moon was split during the time of the Messenger of Allah"
"2251","Narrated by Ḥudhayfah ibn Asīd (may Allāh be pleased with him):\n\nHe said: \The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) appeared upon us from a chamber while we were discussing the Hour (as-Sāʿah). The Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said:\n\n**'The Hour shall not commence until you witness ten signs: the rising of the sun from its place of setting"
"2252","It was narrated from Ubayy bin Ka'b that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\Do not curse the wind. When you see what you dislike"""
"2253","Fatimah bint Qais narrated that Allah's Prophet(s.a.w) ascended the Minbar"
"2254","**Hannād narrated to us:** Abū Mu'āwiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from his father, from Abū Dharr (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:\n\n\I entered the mosque when the sun had set"
"2255","**Narrated by Zainab bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her):**\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) awoke from sleep with his face flushed red, and he was saying: *\Lā ilāha illallāh\""* (There is no god but Allah)"
"2256","Abū Kurayb, Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ, narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us, from ʿĀṣim, from Zirr, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:\n\n\There will emerge at the end of time a people who are young in age and foolish in understanding. They will recite the Qurʾān"
"2257","Abdur-Rahman bin 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated from his father"
"2258","Abu Wa'il narrated from Hudhaifah that 'Umar said:\Which of you remembers what the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said about the Fitnah?\"" So Hudhaifah said: \""I do.\"" Hudhaifah said: \""A man's Fitnah is in his family"""
"2259","'Imran ibn Musa al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us: 'Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an al-Qurashi narrated to us from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in 'Asr prayer one day, then stood up as a preacher. He did not leave anything that will be until the Hour is established except he informed us of it. Whoever memorized it memorized it, and whoever forgot it forgot it. And among what he said: ""Indeed, the world is sweet and green, and Allah is making you successors in it to see how you act. So fear the world and fear women."" And among what he said: ""Let not the awe of people prevent a man from speaking the truth when he knows it."" Abu Sa'id wept and said: ""By Allah, we have seen things and we were awed."" And among what he said: ""Indeed, for every betrayer a banner will be raised on the Day of Resurrection according to his betrayal. And there is no betrayal greater than the betrayal of a general leader; his banner will be planted at his anus."" And among what we memorized that day: ""Indeed, the children of Adam were created in diverse layers. Among them is one who is born a believer, lives a believer, and dies a believer. Among them is one who is born a disbeliever, lives a disbeliever, and dies a disbeliever. Among them is one who is born a believer, lives a believer, and dies a disbeliever. Among them is one who is born a disbeliever, lives a disbeliever, and dies a believer. Indeed, among them is the slow to anger, quick to return (to calmness). And among them is the quick to anger, quick to return. These are equal. Indeed, among them is the quick to anger, slow to return. And the best of them is the slow to anger, quick to return. And the worst of them is the quick to anger, slow to return. Indeed, among them is the good in judgment, good in seeking. And among them is the bad in judgment, good in seeking. And among them is the good in judgment, bad in seeking. These are equal. Indeed, among them is the bad in judgment, bad in seeking. And the best of them is the good in judgment, good in seeking. And the worst of them is the bad in judgment, bad in seeking. Indeed, anger is a coal in the heart of the son of Adam. Do you not see the redness of his eyes and the swelling of his jugular veins? So whoever feels anything of that, let him stick to the ground."" He said: And we turned to look at the sun, has anything of it remained? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Indeed, nothing remains of the world in what has passed of it except like what remains of your day in what has passed of it."" Abu 'Isa said: And in this chapter there are narrations from Hudhayfah, Abu Maryam, Abu Zayd ibn Akhtab, and al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. And they mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ informed them of what will be until the Hour is established. And this is a hasan hadith."
"2260","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\There shall come upon the people a time in which the one who is patient upon his religion will be like the one holding onto a burning ember"""
"2261","Narrated by Abu Hafs, Amr ibn Ali, who narrated from Yahya ibn Said, who narrated from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, who narrated from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not revert to disbelief after me by striking the necks of one another.\"" Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: In this chapter"
"2262","Abu Bakrah said:\Allah restrained me with something that I heard from the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w). When Kisra was destroyed"""
"2263","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) came across some people who were sitting"
"2264","Umar bin Al-Khattab narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:\Shall I not inform you of the best of your leaders and the worst of them: The best of them are those whom you love and they love you"""
"2265","Umm Salamah narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:\Indeed there shall come upon you A'immah whom you like (what they do) and some (of what they do) you dislike. So whoever rejects"""
"2266","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\When your leaders are the best of you"""
"2267","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:\You are in a time when whoever abandons a tenth of what he has been ordered"""
"2268","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) stood on the Minbar and said:\The land of Fitan is there\"" and he pointed to the east"""
"2269","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\Black standards will come from Khurasan"""
"2270","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\When time draws near"""
"2271","Ubadah bin As-Samit narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\The dreams of the believer are a portion of the forty-six portions of Prophet-hood"""
"2272","Anas bin Malik narrated:\The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said: 'Indeed Messenger-ship and Prophethood have been terminated"""
"2273","Ata' bin Yasar narrated from a man among the inhabitants of Egypt who said:I asked Abu Ad-Darda about the saying of Allah"
"2274","Abu Sa'eed narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\The most truthful of dreams are in the last hours of the night"""
"2275","Narrated by Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The Hour shall not come until it is no longer said upon the earth: 'Allah"
"2276","Abdullah narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\Whoever saw me (in a dream) while sleeping then he has indeed seen me. For indeed the Shaitan can not resemble me"""
"2277","Abu Qatadah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Dreams are from Allah and Hulum are from Shaitan. So when one of you sees something that bothers him"""
"2278","Waki' bin 'Udus narrated that Abu Razin Al-'Uqaili said:\ The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said: \"" The believer's dreams are a portion of the forty portions of Prophet-hood. And it is (as if it is) on the leg of a bird"""
"2279","Waki' bin 'Udus narrated from Abu Razin that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\ The Muslim's dreams are a portion of the forty-six portions of Prophet-hood. And it is (as if it is) on the leg of a bird"""
"2280","Abu Hurarirah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Dreams are of three types: The true dream"""
"2281","Abu 'Abdur-Rahman(As-Sulami) narrated from 'Ali and I think he said:\ From the Prophet(s.a.w)"""
"2282","(another chain) from Abu 'Abdur-Rahman As-Sulami who narrated from 'Ali from the Prophet with similar narrations. [He said:This narration is Hasan.] There are narration on this topic from Ibn 'Abbas"
"2283","Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\Whoever lies about having a dream"""
"2284","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\While I was sleeping"""
"2285","Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif narrated from some of the companions of the Prophet (s.a.w) that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:\While I was sleeping I saw people presented before me"""
"2286","Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif narrated from Abu Sa'eed al-Khudri that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:similar in meaning (to no)"
"2287","Abu Bakrah narrated:\One day the Prophet (s.a.w) said: \""'Who among you had a dream?' A man said: \""I did. I saw as if a scale had descended from the Heavens in which you and Abu Bakr were weighed So you outweighed Abu Bakr. Abu Bkar and 'Umar were weighed"""
"2288","Aishah said:\The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) was asked about Waraqah. Khadijah said to him: 'He believed in you"""
"2289","Salim bin 'Abdullah narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Umar about the dream of the Prophet (s.a.w) and Abu Bakr and 'Umar"
"2290","Salim bin 'Abdullah narrated from his father about the dream of the Prophet (s.a.w) who said:\I saw a black woman with unkempt hair going out of Al-Madinah"""
"2291","Abu Hurrairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\In the end of time"""
"2292","Ibn 'abbas narrated fro Abu Hurairah that the Messengr of Allah (s.a.w) said:\I had a dream while sleeping as if there were two gold bracelets in my hands which bothered me very much. So it was reveled to me to blow them off. I blew them off and they flew away. I interpreted thwm to be two liars who would appear after me. One of them caled Masalamah of Yamamah"""
"2293","Abu Hurairah narrated that a man came to the Prophet (s.a.w) and said:\I had a dream of a cloud with shade dripping butter and honey. I saw the people scooping it up with their hands"""
"2294","Samurah bin Jundub narrated :\When the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) had led us in Subh(Fajr prayer)"""
"2295","Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:\Shall l not inform you of the best of witnesses? The one who comes with his testimony before being asked for it"""
"2296","Muhammad ibn Bashshar al-Abdiyy narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafiyy narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The night and the day shall not pass until a man from the freedmen (mawali) shall rule"
"2297","Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:\The best of witnesses is the one who gives his testimony before being asked for it"""
"2298","Aishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:The testimony of a treacherous man is not acceptable nor a treacherous woman nor a man lashed for the Hadd nor a woman lashed nor one possessing malice of enmity nor a rehearsed witness nor the Qani of (one contracted by)the family on their behalf nor the one associating himself to other than his Wala or to other than his relatives"
